WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.750
The creature had a pig's snout and ears.

2
00:00:05.751 --> 00:00:08.881
[g@But he ran on two legs like a person.

3
00:00:08.882 --> 00:00:10.872
He swung the rake again.@g]

4
00:00:10.873 --> 00:00:14.052
Wukong blocked the rake with his iron bar.

5
00:00:14.053 --> 00:00:18.197
[i@Clang!@i] Then he swung the bar at the pig's feet.

6
00:00:18.198 --> 00:00:20.449
[g@"Oof!" cried the pig.

7
00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:23.271
He fell facedown in the dirt.@g]

8
00:00:23.272 --> 00:00:25.050
[g@He jumped back up.

9
00:00:25.051 --> 00:00:28.500
"You'll wish you hadn't done that!"@g]

10
00:00:28.501 --> 00:00:37.688
Wukong leaped out of the way as the pig's rake slammed down, smashing a boulder.

11
00:00:37.689 --> 00:00:43.332
The two fought, kicking up dust and rocks.

12
00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:46.354
The Tang Monk hid behind his horse.

13
00:00:46.355 --> 00:00:51.272
[g@"Surrender now!" Wukong swung his iron bar again.

14
00:00:51.273 --> 00:00:53.452
"I am Sun Wukong.@g]

15
00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:57.348
Five hundred years ago, I caused lots of trouble in Heaven.

16
00:00:57.349 --> 00:01:01.913
The Jade Emperor's entire army couldn't stop me!"

17
00:01:01.914 --> 00:01:04.437
[g@"I've heard of you," said the pig.

18
00:01:04.438 --> 00:01:07.278
"But you don't seem so powerful to me!"@g]

19
00:01:07.279 --> 00:01:09.983
[g@He lunged at the monkey again.

20
00:01:09.984 --> 00:01:12.417
Wukong jumped out of the way.@g]

21
00:01:12.418 --> 00:01:15.510
"I thought you were being punished," said the pig.

22
00:01:15.511 --> 00:01:17.723
[g@He swung his rake again.

23
00:01:17.724 --> 00:01:20.385
"Weren't you trapped under a mountain?"@g]

24
00:01:20.386 --> 00:01:22.950
"I'm free now," said Wukong.

25
00:01:22.951 --> 00:01:25.888
"I'm going to the West with the Tang Monk to—"

26
00:01:25.889 --> 00:01:28.504
[g@"The Tang Monk!" cried the pig.

27
00:01:28.505 --> 00:01:30.722
He dropped his rake.@g]

28
00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:33.261
"I'm supposed to go with him too!"

29
00:01:33.262 --> 00:01:36.550
"You are?" asked Wukong.

30
00:01:36.551 --> 00:01:40.338
"I was sent to Earth as a punishment," said the pig.

31
00:01:40.339 --> 00:01:44.320
[g@"My name is Zhu Bajie.

32
00:01:44.321 --> 00:01:47.174
I caused trouble in Heaven too.@g]

33
00:01:47.175 --> 00:01:54.529
Guanyin said I would be forgiven if I helped protect the Tang Monk."

34
00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:56.605
[g@Wukong rubbed his chin.

35
00:01:56.606 --> 00:02:02.998
"Okay," he said. "You can carry the bags."@g]

36
00:02:02.999 --> 00:02:08.395
Zhu Bajie joined the group, and the three of them continued west.

37
00:02:08.396 --> 00:02:12.551
As they traveled, the pig kept complaining.

38
00:02:12.552 --> 00:02:16.091
[g@"These bags are so heavy!

39
00:02:16.092 --> 00:02:19.338
Do we really need to bring them?"@g]

40
00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:21.872
"Stop complaining," snapped Wukong.

41
00:02:21.873 --> 00:02:26.987
"Going to the Western Paradise is [i@supposed@i] to be difficult."

42
00:02:26.988 --> 00:02:31.081
[g@The pig moaned. "I'm hungry too.

43
00:02:31.082 --> 00:02:33.585
When are we going to eat lunch?"@g]

44
00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:35.687
The Tang Monk frowned.

45
00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:37.611
[g@"We just ate breakfast.

46
00:02:37.612 --> 00:02:40.373
How can you be hungry again?"@g]

47
00:02:40.374 --> 00:02:45.413
They went around a bend and saw a large tiger.

48
00:02:45.414 --> 00:02:49.360
Bajie and Wukong quickly pulled out their weapons.

49
00:02:49.361 --> 00:02:52.119
[g@"Who are you?" yelled Bajie.

50
00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:54.754
"What are you doing here?"@g]

51
00:02:54.755 --> 00:03:01.123
"My master, the great king Yellow Wind, is hosting a feast," said the tiger.

52
00:03:01.124 --> 00:03:04.073
[g@He looked at the Tang Monk.

53
00:03:04.074 --> 00:03:07.559
"I'm gathering people to eat."@g]

54
00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:12.749
The Tang Monk's face turned pale, and he fell off his horse.

55
00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:16.616
"Don't you dare harm our master!" Bajie warned.

56
00:03:16.617 --> 00:03:18.366
[g@"He is the Tang Monk.

57
00:03:18.367 --> 00:03:21.994
He's going to the West to get the True Scriptures."@g]

58
00:03:21.995 --> 00:03:24.805
The tiger's eyes opened wide.

59
00:03:24.806 --> 00:03:29.814
"I heard that eating the Tang Monk will make someone live forever."

60
00:03:29.815 --> 00:03:33.383
[g@The tiger showed his claws.

61
00:03:33.384 --> 00:03:35.945
Then he lunged at Bajie.@g]

62
00:03:35.946 --> 00:03:38.242
[g@The pig hit him with the rake.

63
00:03:38.243 --> 00:03:40.937
The tiger tumbled over.@g]

64
00:03:40.938 --> 00:03:44.479
Wukong ran toward the tiger with his iron bar.

65
00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:49.079
The tiger dodged the bar and then almost got hit by the rake again.

66
00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:51.845
He turned and fled.

67
00:03:51.846 --> 00:03:57.332
[g@Wukong and Bajie ran after the tiger.

68
00:03:57.333 --> 00:04:00.195
For a moment they lost him.@g]

69
00:04:00.196 --> 00:04:05.166
Then they spotted a flash of orange behind some bushes.

70
00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:08.364
"There he is!" whispered Bajie.

71
00:04:08.365 --> 00:04:11.907
The monkey and pig sneaked up to the bushes.

72
00:04:11.908 --> 00:04:14.113
[g@But the tiger wasn't there.

73
00:04:14.114 --> 00:04:21.657
Instead a tiger skin lay over a rock.@g]

74
00:04:21.658 --> 00:04:27.323
Wukong laughed. "He was so scared, he ran right out of his skin!"

75
00:04:27.324 --> 00:04:29.685
[g@He slapped Bajie on the back.

76
00:04:29.686 --> 00:04:34.618
"We are great protectors!"@g]

77
00:04:34.619 --> 00:04:39.399
The two friends walked back to the road, laughing.

78
00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:42.714
But suddenly their laughter stopped.

79
00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:51.828
"Oh no!" cried Wukong. "Where is the Tang Monk?"

